<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12906" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπο-κοπή</span></b> , ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποκόπτω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>cutting off,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρατός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					841
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Mochl.</u>
				34
			</span></i>; <i>lopping off</i> a shoot <i>for grafting,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				M.Ant.
				11.8
			</span></i>: Medic., <i>amputation,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Archig.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				47.13.3
			</span></i>; <i>stoppage,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμμηίνων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Sor.
					1.26
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πεδίων ἀ.,</span> prob.their <i>abrupt
				terminations,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Phil.</u>
				4
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Gp.</u>
				12.41.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φωνῆς ἀ.</span>
			<i>loss</i> of voice, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				2.120
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				13.31
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποκοπαζ χρεῶν</span>
			<i>cancelling</i> of all debts, <i><span class="en">
				And.
				1.88
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				566a
			</span></i>, Jusj. ap. <i><span class="en">
				D.
				24.149
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>abruptness,</i> esp. of literary style, <i><span class="en">
				Demetr.
				<u>Eloc.</u>
				238
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ῥυθμοῦ</span>
			<i>broken</i> rhythm, ib.<i><span class="en">
				6
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξ ἀποκοπῆς</span>”
				<i>abruptly,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					<u>Th.</u>
					52
				</span></i>
			; also of disease, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξ ἀ.
			λυθῆναι</span> to be <i>suddenly</i> cured, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				7.441
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			<i>section, extract,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόγου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Tryph.
					<u>Trop.</u>
					7
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>V.</b> in Gramm.,
				<i>apocope, cutting off of</i> one or more letters, esp. at
			the end of a word, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Po.</u>
				1458b2
			</span></i> (pl.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				A.D.
				<u>Synt.</u>
				6.11
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατ᾽ ἀποκοπήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					8.5.3
				</span></i>
			; also of elliptical expressions, such as <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νὴ τόν,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				2.271
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
